This is what produced my stupid action.  I realized that even a
luckstone would not move in a corner where you cannot but kick it
against a wall.  But I believed it would not hurt, rather, it would just
stay in place, possibly with some other funny message.  So I thought
*this* was the loadstone and went to all the other chambers where I had
been. In one of them was, of course, another gray stone.  I kicked it
and just got the answer "thump".  Which is not as bad as "ouch that
hurts", IMO.  So I picked the stone up and it was the loadstone.  I
should have realized that behind this stone there *was* a free space, so
it *would* have moved had it been a luckstone. 

Since I was carrying a large box for lack of a bag, I could get from
stressed to burdened by just dropping it.  I then backtracked to Dlvl 1,
where I remembered two fountains, one of which had earlier helped me to
get rid of fumble boots (on which my pet had stepped apparently without
the usual "... moves only reluctantly", or I simply missed it).  I
dipped the stone into one fountain, which gave me a gem and finally
dried out.  Then I dipped it into the other, got another gem, but later
also the message about the glowing water.  So I got rid of the
loadstone, which I had named in the meantime.

Back at mines' bottom I inspected the other stone.  Sure enough, it was
still a gray stone, not a loadstone.  So I picked it up, and it did not
burden me.  Hence I suppose, it is the luckstone.  Of course, I got
burdened again, taking my valuable large box along.

